# Kin v1.0 epic rules

Read `projects/kin/AGENTS.md` first, including its "Cursor Cloud specific instructions" section. Everything there applies. This file is the short version for the v1.0 epic.

## Scope
- Only change files under `projects/kin/`. Never edit `.cursor/`, `.github/`, `REVIEW.md` or the root `README.md`.
- One issue per branch and per PR. Base and target: `kin-development`. Branch name: `kin-v1/<issue-number>-<short-slug>`.
- Do only what the issue asks. File anything else you notice as a note in the PR body under "Deferred". Don't fix it.
- If the issue's "Blocked by" issues aren't merged yet, stop and say so.
- If the issue leaves a product decision open (for example S1's archived-area note rule), comment on the issue and stop. Don't pick an answer.

## Hard rules
- Zero dependencies: no crates, npm packages, CDN scripts or vendored code. Use the Rust std library and web platform APIs only.
- Never merge, tag, release, deploy or force-push a shared branch.
- Don't change golden fixtures, the KINE/KINS formats, the WASM ABI or the IndexedDB schema unless the issue says to. If you must, say so at the top of the PR body.
- Keep replay deterministic: order by `(logical_time, device_id, event_id)`, with no clocks, randomness or hash-map iteration order in Rust domain logic.
- Security fixes come with a regression test that fails before the fix and passes after it.
- Do not edit `.nvmrc`, `create-issues.sh` or anything under `projects/kin/config/` unless the issue says to.

## Verify before every push
From `projects/kin/`:
```sh
./build-wasm.sh
cargo test --offline
node --test server/*.test.mjs
node scripts/verify.mjs
```
The Edge browser suites run only in Windows CI. Report them as "CI only" and never claim a pass you didn't see.

## Answering the Claude review
- 🔴 Important: fix it, or reply with `file:line` evidence that it's wrong.
- 🟡 Nit: fix it if cheap; otherwise reply with a one-line reason.
- 🟣 Pre-existing: don't fix it in this PR. List it under "Deferred".
- Don't resolve review threads. The owner does that.
- After pushing fixes, comment `/kin-review` on the PR to request a re-review.

## PR body
Use the Agent Completion Format from `projects/kin/AGENTS.md` and add:
- `Closes #<issue>`
- each acceptance criterion from the issue, ticked, with the test that proves it
- the exact commands you ran and their results
